Z||000000||1FieroGTRacingInc||01-03-2001||12:26 AM||||I need everybody's input on this...  I found a 84 2m4 with a 4-speed in it...  It has 84k on it. I can get a 6 month warranty w/ it... I can get the axel's, pedal's cables..  etc.  everything that I will need...<BR>I have an automatic now (yucko) I can get everything for $200.00 with the 6 month warranty.  Is this a good deal or not ???<BR>what do I need   thanks steve||||reg||5
Z||000001||Oreif||01-03-2001||02:02 AM||||On my first 86 SE I had the 4-spd and I liked it alot. From what I understand the 84 4-spd had a 4.11 gearing where 85 and 86 they cut it down to mid 3.something. If you drive a lot of highway time I'd look for the 5-spd. If you drive locally and enjoy the occasional stoplight to stoplight sprints, Go "4" it.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||Standard||01-03-2001||03:56 AM||||84's had two choices for final drive, a 4.10 performance ratio with an RPO code of M19, and a 3.32 economy ratio with an RPO code of MY8.  Both at completly different ends of the spectrum as far as acceleration goes.  If you do any kind of highway driving I would stay away from the 4.10.. and you better have a pretty modded v6 if you want any kind of acceleration out of the 3.32..<P>The 85-86 4 speeds used a 3.65 ratio, and had an RPO code of M17<p>[This message has been edited by Standard (edited 01-03-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||Cooter||01-03-2001||06:44 PM||||I have the m19 with my 3.4 and I love it! I do no highway driving with the car, so the deep gears are not a concern. If I had some extra money, I believe that I would take one of my Isuzu's and add a 3.73 ring/pinion to it. I believe that would be an excellant compromise between acceleration/economy.||||reg||1
